.TH NOWAYPROMPT.CONF 5 2026-07-26 nowayprompt "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
nowayprompt.conf \- nowayprompt configuration format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I base/nowayprompt/config.ini
.br
.I base/wayprompt/config.ini
.P
where
.I base
is the first non-empty of
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME ,
.IR $HOME/.config ,
and
.IR /etc .
.SH DESCRIPTION
nowayprompt reads at most one configuration file. It confines the lookup to a
single base directory:
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
when set and non-empty, otherwise
.I $HOME/.config
when
.I $HOME
is set and non-empty, otherwise
.IR /etc .
Within that base,
.I nowayprompt/config.ini
is the primary candidate and
.I wayprompt/config.ini
is the fallback; the first candidate that exists wins. An empty primary file
counts as existing and is loaded. The fallback is consulted silently, files
are never merged, candidates outside the selected base are never consulted,
and an existing file that cannot be read or parsed is reported as an error
instead of being skipped. An absent configuration file is not an error:
built-in defaults are used.
.P
The file format is the
.BR wayprompt (5)
INI dialect: assignments sorted into
.B [general]
and
.B [colours]
sections. General settings configure Wayland geometry and fonts. Colours use
0xRRGGBB or 0xRRGGBBAA values. Runtime labels, TTY names, and Wayland display
selection are supplied by the invoking command or Assuan protocol and are not
configuration-file keys.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nowayprompt (1),
.BR pinentry-nowayprompt (1),
.BR wayprompt (5)
